N1  - Deseret Evening News, October 29, 1870, p. 2. “Correspondence between Lieutenant-General D. H. Wells and Governor J. W. Shaffer,” with “Letter from Lieutenant-General D. H. Wells.” A quarrel over the territorial militia. Governor Shaffer had banned musters and refused to recognize Wells as its lieutenant-general. To show that earlier governors had recognized him, Wells printed Acting Governor Frank Fuller’s order of June 11, 1862, requiring him to furnish Marshal Henry W. Lawrence and his deputies Burton and McKean with “a sufficient military force” to arrest Joseph Morris. That is the earliest printing of the order found for this guide. Other links: Transcription on morrisite.org: https://morrisite.org/documents.html#dn-1870-10-29 Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1870
