TY  - NEWS
TI  - Railroad Meeting at Gwendale
T2  - New North-West
PY  - 1875
DA  - 1875/04/16/
SP  - 2
UR  - https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1875-04-16/ed-1/?sp=2
KW  - Burton’s arrest and trial, 1877–1879
N1  - New North-West, April 16, 1875, p. 2. “Railroad Meeting at Gwendale.” Also June 18, 1875, p. 3; September 8, 1876, p. 3; July 6, 1877, p. 3; August 31, 1877, p. 3; April 30, 1880, p. 4; January 20, 1882, p. 3; March 10, 1882, p. 3; May 4, 1883, p. 3. Notices that place Gwendale, later Morristown, in the upper Deer Lodge valley. The April 1875 mass meeting of “the citizens of Upper Deer Lodge Valley” at the Gwendale school house was chaired by Morgan Evans, with W. Watkin Thomas on the resolutions committee. Primaries were held at Wier’s store (1875); the 1876 election judges for Gwendale were Morgan Evans, Peter Jessen and Wm Wier; a W W Thomas of Gwendale paid a subscription (1877); and a fifty-ton smelter at Gwendale began work in August 1877. A land-office notice of March 1880 lists Warm Springs settlers whose homestead claims awaited a hearing on whether the land was mineral, among them Daniel James, William P. Thomas, Morgan Evans and Peter Jessen. In January 1882 John R. Eardley built a store at “Daniel James’ corner, Warm Springs settlement,” and in March he was appointed postmaster “at Willow Glen on Warm Spring creek, where the Gwendale postoffice formerly was.” By 1883 school district No. 6 was called Willow Glen. None of these items calls anyone a Morrisite. Other links: June 18, 1875: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1875-06-18/ed-1/?sp=3; Sept. 8, 1876: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1876-09-08/ed-1/?sp=3; July 6, 1877: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1877-07-06/ed-1/?sp=3; Aug. 31, 1877: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1877-08-31/ed-1/?sp=3; Apr. 30, 1880: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1880-04-30/ed-1/?sp=4; Jan. 20, 1882: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1882-01-20/ed-1/?sp=3; Mar. 10, 1882: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1882-03-10/ed-1/?sp=3; May 4, 1883: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1883-05-04/ed-1/?sp=3 Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1877
