KW  - 1880–1900 and the 1891 letters
N1  - New North-West, July 11, 1884, p. 3. “Reorganized Latter-day Saints.” Notice of W. W. Blair’s RLDS preaching at the Deer Lodge courthouse; the church, “like that of the Josephites and Morrisites,” is distinct from Brigham Young’s and opposed to polygamy. It names the church’s Montana congregations: at Rees Creek near Bozeman, at Willow Creek near Gallatin City, and “near Stuart, in upper Deer Lodge valley.” The Reese Creek branch in Gallatin County was the first in Montana, founded in 1868 by the missionary Joseph W. Morgan, who baptized John E. Reese there (Don Cornelius, “Mormonism in Montana, 1847–1898,” M.A. thesis, 1962, p. 56). Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1891
