N1  - New North-West, November 13, 1885, p. 3. “Notice. To all Whom It May Concern.” The Montana church disowns the Doves: two men “calling themselves ‘Doves,’” claiming to be Morrisites, are warned against as “pretenders” by the leaders of the church organized in the county “under the name of the ‘Church of the Saints of the Most High,’” who “utterly repudiate their claims, teachings and practices.” Signed William M. James, Andrew Hendrickson and John R. Eardley. The council had ordered the notice at its meeting of November 10 (Church History Library, MS 32226, minutebook, pp. 25–27). Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1891
