PY  - 1886
DA  - 1886/09/03/
SP  - 3
UR  - https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1886-09-03/ed-1/?sp=3
KW  - 1880–1900 and the 1891 letters
N1  - New North-West, September 3, 1886, p. 3. Also February 19 and March 26, 1886, p. 3. “A Mormon Church, of the Morrisite branch, we are informed, is being constructed under the superintendence of Elder Clapp on the Cottonwood road about a half mile east of town.” An Elder J. C. Clapp had preached at the Deer Lodge court house in February and March 1886, once on the “Origin of the American Indians,” a Book of Mormon theme. The Morrisites’ own minutes settle the question: in November 1886 their council recorded an invitation from “Elder Clapp of the Reorganized Church” to use that church’s meeting house at Deer Lodge City while he was preaching in Utah (Church History Library, MS 32226, minutebook, pp. 37–38). The building was the Reorganized Church’s, not a Morrisite church; Clapp was very probably the RLDS missionary Joseph C. Clapp. Other links: Chronicling America: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1886-02-19/ed-1/?sp=3; Chronicling America: https://www.loc.gov/resource/sn84038125/1886-03-26/ed-1/?sp=3 Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1891
